I've been experimenting with removing the `flex-1` spacer, and the results are promising. By adjusting the flex properties of the opponent area and location info, I can ensure they are properly spaced and positioned within the flex container. I'm aiming for a layout where the top and bottom sections are neatly aligned without relying on an intermediary spacer. This approach addresses the previously noted padding issues and aligns with the overall board layout cleanup goals.


